ckernel.cpp ScanPannelKey, the four ALARM RESET checks (front pad :3369/:3377, rear pad :3581/:3588; golden runs them last so
they overwrite ret, and the bK latch then returns -1 every scan while the key is held => every other key is lost; pad log
09:15:57 t050400002020 = HOME + stuck RESET). Now the Sen part only takes over when nothing else was pressed (ret==-1) or the
RESET latch bK[SnFKAlarmReset (+SnRKPowerOff on the rear pad)] is not yet set, i.e. a fresh RESET press still wins exactly as
golden, a held one gives way. bAseAlarmReset (soft reset) unchanged. Same lines.
tests/test_scankey_golden.cpp: new block before the end -- fresh RESET -> RESET; held -> -1; HOME while RESET held -> HOME;
both fresh together -> RESET.
ScanKeyGolden, MainScanKey, W7_L2_CKernel, SysinitBoot, St02_N07Alarm, St02_PadInterface passed. Debug and release wb_serve
linked. Backup D:\HT9045\_review\ckernel.cpp.bak_rstheld_20261007_172605. WORKLOG row 171.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
